My best interpretation of the umask rules for symbolic modes:
- Starting mode: 0777
- `+` with omitted who: add bits, but only bits not in umask (for ordinary bits); special bits (s, t) are always added
- `-` with omitted who: remove bits, but only bits not in umask (for ordinary bits); special bits (s, t) are always removed
- `=` with omitted who: set ordinary bits to (requested & ~umask); special bits are set as requested
- `+`/`-`/`=` with explicit who (u, g, o, a): no umask effect at all

